      "instance_name": "shocked_reaction_scene",
      "label": "elderly_man_showing_shocked_reaction",
      "description": "The scene depicts an elderly man with a highly exaggerated facial expression of shock or alarm, which is juxtaposed with the text 'help refugees' to create an emotional and propagandistic visual impact. The man's expression is the central visual element, and the text serves as a direct call to action, creating a scene of emotional appeal and moral urgency.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_085c42b9"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_be2e5e40",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "background_knowledge_item_1",
      "label": "The man in the image is a known public figure",
      "description": "The elderly man depicted in the image is not a random individual but a recognizable public figure, specifically the Polish-American actor and comedian Frank Caliendo. His exaggerated facial expression is a signature part of his comedic persona, often used in political satire and impersonations. Recognizing him as Frank Caliendo is essential to understanding the meme’s context — it is not merely a generic shocked face, but a specific comedic performance being repurposed for a political or humanitarian message. This knowledge is outside the image and required to interpret the meme’s intent and cultural reference.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_085c42b9"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2c7dd757",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "background_knowledge_item_2",
      "label": "Frank Caliendo’s comedic style and political satire",
      "description": "Frank Caliendo is known for his exaggerated facial expressions and vocal impressions, often used to satirize political figures and current events. His style is rooted in political comedy and impersonation, which makes his shocked expression a tool for comedic effect rather than genuine emotion. Understanding this context is necessary to interpret the meme — the juxtaposition of his comedic reaction with the serious plea 'help refugees' is a form of satirical or ironic commentary, not a literal emotional appeal. This background knowledge is required to understand the meme’s tone and intent.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_085c42b9"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_4e9e3fc4",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "background_knowledge_item_3",
      "label": "The use of 'help refugees' as a political slogan or call to action",
      "description": "The phrase 'help refugees' is a common humanitarian slogan used in political discourse, media campaigns, and social movements. It is often employed to mobilize public support for refugee aid policies, international relief efforts, or to critique government inaction. Understanding the political and social context of this phrase — its frequent use in debates over immigration, asylum, and international aid — is necessary to interpret the meme’s propagandistic intent. This knowledge is outside the image and required to understand the message being conveyed.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_085c42b9"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_ebaef45d",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "background_knowledge_item_4",
      "label": "The meme format of using a shocked reaction to frame a political or social issue",
      "description": "This meme leverages a common internet meme format where a person’s exaggerated reaction (often comedic or absurd) is used to frame a serious or controversial issue. The format is designed to create a sense of urgency or moral outrage by juxtaposing an emotional response with a call to action. Understanding this meme format — its history, usage, and cultural significance — is necessary to interpret the meme’s intent and effectiveness. This background knowledge is required to understand the visual and rhetorical strategy being employed.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_085c42b9"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e87b6648",
      "@type": "EmotionExpression",
      "instance_name": "shock",
      "label": "the shocked emotion",
      "description": "The elderly man's facial expression, characterized by wide eyes and a slightly open mouth, conveys a strong sense of shock or alarm. This exaggerated reaction is central to the meme's visual impact and is used to evoke an emotional response from viewers, intended to frame the issue of refugee aid as an urgent crisis.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_085c42b9"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_99124998",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
      "label": "The text 'help refugees' is mapped onto the visual of the elderly man's shocked reaction.",
      "description": "The meme uses the visual of the elderly man's exaggerated shocked expression to analogically represent the emotional urgency or moral outrage implied by the text 'help refugees'. The mapping is not literal (the man is not literally calling for help), but rather rhetorical: his reaction is projected as the visual embodiment of the emotional response the text seeks to provoke. This is a common meme format where a person's reaction is used to frame a serious issue as an immediate crisis requiring action. The man's expression is mapped onto the text's call to action, creating a visual metaphor for the perceived gravity of the refugee situation.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_085c42b9"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_6caa3901",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the visual material of the elderly man's shocked reaction",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the elderly man (elderly_man) displaying an exaggerated shocked expression. This projection is implicit, as the meme format relies on the viewer identifying with the emotional intensity of the reaction to internalize the urgency of the text 'help refugees'. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the visual framing invites the user to mentally inhabit the role of the reacting subject, thereby projecting their own emotional response onto the scene. The user is projected onto the visual material (elderly_man) which serves as the emotional anchor for the textual message.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_085c42b9"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_16fb0fc9",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "general public",
      "description": "The meme is designed to appeal to a broad, general public audience, particularly those engaged with current events, humanitarian issues, or political discourse. The use of a widely recognizable public figure (Frank Caliendo) and a common humanitarian slogan ('help refugees') ensures accessibility and immediate recognition, allowing the meme to resonate with viewers across various demographics who are familiar with internet meme culture and political satire. The propagandistic intent targets individuals who are emotionally responsive to visual cues and moral appeals, aiming to mobilize them toward supporting refugee aid.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_085c42b9"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    }
